{'_client': <twikit.client.client.Client object at 0x000001E534E2AE40>, '_data': {'__typename': 'Tweet', 'rest_id': '1877408824111649076', 'core': {'user_results': {'result': {'__typename': 'User', 'id': 'VXNlcjoxMTE1NzQ5NjMzOTg3MzA1NDcy', 'rest_id': '1115749633987305472', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': True, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Tue Apr 09 22:53:37 +0000 2019', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': 'Retired Royal Canadian Marine Search & Rescue Specialist. Happily married to a compassionate and dedicated frontline Doctor with 3  amazing, talented children.', 'entities': {'description': {'urls': []}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 197141, 'followers_count': 11915, 'friends_count': 9798, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 8, 'location': '', 'media_count': 5181, 'name': 'Barry Sharp', 'normal_followers_count': 11915, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1878838948962951297'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1115749633987305472/1722786870', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1820126123474538496/wurAA1jZ_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'BarryESharp', 'statuses_count': 199826, 'translator_type': 'none', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1877408824111649076'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1736447718000', 'is_edit_eligible': False, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '86', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="http://twitter.com/download/iphone" rel="nofollow">Twitter for iPhone</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4Nzc0MDg4MjM4MjYzMjk2MDA=', 'text': "Unraveling the Mystery: Why Don't We Know the Causes of Vaccine-Related Adverse Events?\n\nAs we mark four years since the rollout of synthetic mRNA and DNA vaccines, a pressing question lingers in the public health discourse: why don’t we fully understand the mechanisms behind the adverse events associated with these vaccines, such as myocarditis, pericarditis, thrombosis, strokes, and even death? The urgency of this inquiry cannot be overstated, especially given the profound implications for vaccine safety and public trust.\n\nAt the core of this issue lies the unique technology employed in these vaccines. Synthetic mRNA and DNA shots utilize lipid nanoparticles to deliver genetic material into cells, triggering an immune response. However, these nanoparticles may also introduce unintended consequences. The complexity of this technology raises several critical questions regarding safety mechanisms and the potential for harm.\n\n1. Lipid Nanoparticles: These carriers are essential for delivering mRNA into cells, but their interactions with human biology are not entirely understood. Could the lipid nanoparticles themselves provoke inflammatory responses or other adverse effects?\n\n2. DNA Template Contamination: The presence of contaminants in DNA templates used in these vaccines raises concerns. If these contaminants can elicit immune responses or disrupt normal cellular processes, they could contribute to serious health issues.\n\n3. Modified Pseudouridine Stability: Modified nucleotides like pseudouridine are designed to enhance the stability of mRNA. However, if these modifications do not degrade as intended, they may lead to prolonged immune activation or other unforeseen consequences.\n\n4. Adenoviral Vectors: Vaccines such as those from AstraZeneca and Johnson & Johnson utilize a chimpanzee adenovirus (Ad26) as a vector. While this method is effective for vaccine delivery, it is essential to consider whether the vector itself can induce adverse immune reactions.\n\nAdding to the complexity is the fact that many individuals received mixed vaccine doses, further complicating any analysis of safety profiles. Observational studies conducted to assess the efficacy and safety of these vaccines can often only establish correlations, not causations. This lack of causal evidence makes it difficult to pinpoint specific mechanisms of harm.\n\nMoreover, as time passes, the opportunity to investigate long-term effects diminishes. Many adverse events may not become apparent until years later, leading to a potentially skewed perception of safety. The lack of interest in thoroughly investigating vaccine-related deaths further complicates our understanding, leaving many questions unanswered.\n\nThe scientific community must prioritize further investigation into these adverse events to regain public trust and ensure vaccine safety. Transparent research is necessary to explore the underlying causes of harm linked to these vaccines. Only through rigorous inquiry can we hope to understand the complexities and risks associated with synthetic mRNA and DNA technology.\n\nAs we reflect on the past four years, it is crucial to ask not only why we lack answers but also how we can move forward. Addressing these gaps in knowledge is essential for public health, vaccine development, and ultimately, the well-being of society. The questions may be uncomfortable, but they are necessary for fostering a safer and more informed future.", 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}}}}, 'legacy': {'bookmark_count': 0, 'bookmarked': False, 'created_at': 'Thu Jan 09 17:35:18 +0000 2025', 'conversation_id_str': '1877347490887811322', 'display_text_range': [14, 294], 'entities': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'timestamps': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': [{'id_str': '69156861', 'name': 'Chief Nerd', 'screen_name': 'TheChiefNerd', 'indices': [0, 13]}]}, 'favorite_count': 1, 'favorited': False, 'full_text': "@TheChiefNerd Unrav